WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.433
Welcome back, creators!

00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:09.433
Last time, we built the structure

00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:12.767
of Number Match with HTML.

00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:18.133
Today, we start turning this plain page... into this!

00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:22.033
This is the power of CSS.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.867
CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets.

00:00:26.867 --> 00:00:29.333
It controls how our webpage looks:

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:34.600
the colours, the sizes, the spacing, and even the movement.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.367
Click the new file button,

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:40.933
type style.css, and press Enter.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.833
We keep our styles in their own file.

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:48.300
That way, HTML looks after the structure,

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:53.400
CSS looks after the style, and everything stays tidy.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.033
Now go back to index.html.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:59.200
Inside the <head>, just before the

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.933
closing </head> tag, type this link.

00:01:03.733 --> 00:01:06.900
rel="stylesheet" tells the browser

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.333
that this is a style file.

00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:14.000
And href tells it where to find it: style.css.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:18.500
Let's write our first CSS rule.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:21.233
First comes the selector.

00:01:21.233 --> 00:01:25.000
It tells the browser which elements we want to style.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.133
Here, we choose the body.

00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:31.267
Then a pair of curly brackets.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:35.600
Everything inside them is called a declaration block.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:39.867
Inside, we write a property, a colon, and a value.

00:01:39.867 --> 00:01:42.567
background-color is the property,

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:45.767
and this colour code is the value.

00:01:45.933 --> 00:01:48.900
And every declaration ends with a semicolon,

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:52.467
like a full stop at the end of a sentence.

00:01:52.867 --> 00:01:57.833
The second declaration sets our font-family to Quicksand.

00:01:57.833 --> 00:02:03.133
But wait! The browser needs to download Quicksand first.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.633
Websites can use thousands of different fonts.

00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:11.333
Many of them are free on Google Fonts.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:16.233
Open your browser and go to fonts.google.com.

00:02:16.633 --> 00:02:20.567
Search for Quicksand, and click on it.

00:02:20.967 --> 00:02:25.067
Click Get font, and then Get embed code.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:28.300
Make sure the weights we need are

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.600
chosen, from 400 up to 700.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.700
The higher the number, the bolder the text.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:39.300
Now copy the link code that Google gives us.

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:43.067
Back in Paisley Studio, paste it inside the

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:46.167
<head>, above our stylesheet link.

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:49.733
The two preconnect lines help the font load quickly,

00:02:49.733 --> 00:02:53.733
and the last link downloads Quicksand itself.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.367
Remember: the browser needs an internet

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:59.867
connection to download a Google Font.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:05.300
Now let's build our design, starting with our colours.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.567
At the very top of style.css,

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:13.000
we create CSS variables, inside :root.

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:17.067
A variable is a colour with a name.

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:23.633
--green is our deep forest green. --red is our bright red.

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:26.567
To use a variable, we write var(),

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:29.500
with the name inside the brackets.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.833
Here's why that's so clever.

00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:36.767
If we change --red in one place...

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:41.233
...every part of the design that uses it changes too!

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.500
Next, the page and the header.

00:03:45.867 --> 00:03:49.367
The .app-shell keeps our game a comfortable width,

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:52.800
and margin: 0 auto places it in the middle.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.100
The .topbar uses display:

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.900
flex, which lines things up in a row.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:01.467
justify-content: space-between pushes the brand

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:04.767
to the left, and the tag to the right.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:06.800
The heading becomes big,

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:11.500
bold and green, and the span inside it turns red.

00:04:11.867 --> 00:04:14.300
The game panel gets a white background,

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.667
a border, and rounded corners.

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:19.933
The stats use display:

00:04:19.933 --> 00:04:24.500
grid, with three equal columns, one for each box.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.667
And the progress fill is red.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:30.767
Its width starts at zero percent.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:34.500
Later, JavaScript will make it grow.

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:39.033
Now for my favourite part: the number card.

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:41.933
Our grid is still empty, because JavaScript

00:04:41.933 --> 00:04:44.933
will create the cards in a later lesson.

00:04:44.933 --> 00:04:49.300
So let's zoom in and design one card right now.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.867
We start with a white rectangle.

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:56.600
border-radius rounds the corners.

00:04:56.767 --> 00:05:01.300
Then a thick red border, five pixels wide.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.667
Inside, the number circle.

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:06.267
Its width and height are equal,

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:11.700
and border-radius: 50% turns a square into a perfect circle.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:15.100
background-color makes it red.

00:05:15.267 --> 00:05:17.300
display: grid and place-items:

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:20.667
center put the number exactly in the middle.

00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:23.600
font-size makes the number large,

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.900
and font-weight: 700 makes it bold.

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:31.000
And finally, the number word underneath.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:35.067
Here's our card next to the original design.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:39.033
The same bold style, made with code!

00:05:39.433 --> 00:05:41.833
The game grid places our cards in four

00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:45.233
columns, with a gap between them.

00:05:46.233 --> 00:05:49.400
But how do the cards flip over?

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:55.200
Every card has two faces: a green back, and a white front.

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:59.267
transform: rotateY(180deg) spins an

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:03.500
element around, like turning a page.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.567
The front starts already turned around,

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:11.667
and backface-visibility: hidden makes the side facing away invisible.

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:14.867
When a card gets the class is-flipped,

00:06:14.867 --> 00:06:18.833
the inside turns around, and the number appears.

00:06:19.233 --> 00:06:23.300
The transition makes the turn smooth instead of sudden.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:26.667
It takes just over half a second.

00:06:27.033 --> 00:06:30.200
And when a pair matches, the class is-matched

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:33.267
turns the border and the circle green.

00:06:34.267 --> 00:06:36.067
Last one.

00:06:36.067 --> 00:06:37.500
People will play our game on

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.167
computers, tablets and phones.

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:44.067
A media query lets us change

00:06:44.067 --> 00:06:47.200
styles when the screen is small.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.467
max-width: 650px means:

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:54.167
only on screens 650 pixels wide or narrower.

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:57.967
On small screens, the cards get thinner borders,

00:06:57.967 --> 00:07:03.400
smaller gaps, and smaller numbers, so everything still fits.

00:07:03.567 --> 00:07:06.900
That's called responsive design.

00:07:07.867 --> 00:07:10.800
Look at what we have created!

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:15.167
Our simple page is now becoming a beautiful game.

00:07:15.567 --> 00:07:19.433
But our cards still need something important.

00:07:19.633 --> 00:07:22.200
They need a brain.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:24.367
Next, we are going to introduce

00:07:24.367 --> 00:07:28.433
JavaScript, and teach our game how to think!
